WHAT: Adds #[arithmetic(unchecked)] to SolEncoder's finish() and write_word_at()
methods.

WHY: finish() computes end - start (can't underflow, end >= start by construction).
write_word_at() does a plain mstore with no arithmetic. Both had redundant
overflow checks.

GAS IMPACT: Mixed, small. -465 gas total across contracts.
  amm: -113 to -117
  math: -15 to -17
  escrow: -12 to -17
  governance: -6 to -27
  erc20: +12 to +15 (small regression from code layout effects)

CODEGEN IMPACT: Removes 2 uaddo instructions from encoder paths. The erc20
regression is likely a code layout artifact (different instruction ordering
changes JUMPDEST positions).

TEAM NOTES: Diminishing returns on unchecked annotations. The big wins (steps
15, 16, 18) already captured the high-frequency paths. Encoder paths are
called less often than decoder paths (decode happens on every call, encode
only on return/events).
